IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-s7-base`
IMPORT `ccc1-s7-aircraft-platforms-ships`

-- ccc1-tests-s7-aircraft-platforms-ships.l4 -- tests for section 7(1) to (2.21) of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the subsection named beside each group. Arguments are positional, in GIVEN order.
-- The offence is named by its section (and subsection or paragraph) as the core record `Provision of the Code`.

`ccc1 test section 76` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 76, ""
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(a)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(a)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(b)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(b)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(c)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(c)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(d)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(d)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(e)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(e)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(f)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(f)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(g)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(g)"
`ccc1 test paragraph 77(h)` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, "(h)"
`ccc1 test whole section 77` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 77, ""
`ccc1 test section 78.1` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 78.1, ""
`ccc1 test itself` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission would be the offence itself`
`ccc1 test conspiracy` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission would be a conspiracy to commit the offence`
`ccc1 test attempt` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission would be an attempt to commit the offence`
`ccc1 test accessory` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission would be being an accessory after the fact to the offence`
`ccc1 test counselling` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission would be counselling in relation to the offence`
`ccc1 test no relation` MEANS `s 7 the act or omission has none of those relations to the offence`

§ `s 7(1)  (the aircraft; in flight by s 7(8); the flight terminated in Canada; the class of the offence)`
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(a)(i) an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(i): registered in Canada, in flight; where the flight ended does not matter
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(a)(ii) an aircraft leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft registered in Canada under those regulations` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(ii), and an offence that is also punishable by indictment
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(b) any other aircraft` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): any aircraft in flight, the flight having terminated in Canada
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(b) any other aircraft` (JUST TRUE) FALSE `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b): "if the flight terminated in Canada" is not met
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(a)(i) an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not in flight: "while the aircraft is in flight"
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(b) any other aircraft` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b), not in flight
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(a)(i) an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act` NOTHING TRUE `an indictable offence` EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 7(8) did not answer: carried through
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1) not an aircraft` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `an indictable offence` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on or in respect of an aircraft: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` `s 7(1)(a)(i) an aircraft registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `an offence punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING   -- an offence punishable only on summary conviction is not "an offence punishable by indictment"

§ `s 7(2)  (outside Canada; circumstance; offence; relation; in flight by s 7(8); in service by s 7(9); present in Canada)`
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): on an aircraft in flight, an offence against section 76, the person present in Canada after
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(a)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): paragraph 77(a)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(c)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- 77(c) is a paragraph (b) offence, not an offence of paragraph (a): not covered
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a): not in flight, "while the aircraft is in flight"
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test itself` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 7(8) did not answer
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(c)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): paragraph 77(c), aircraft in service
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(d)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): paragraph 77(d)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(g)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b): paragraph 77(g)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(c)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b): the aircraft is not in service, so not "in relation to an aircraft in service"
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(b) in relation to an aircraft in service` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(c)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 7(9) did not answer
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(c) in relation to an air navigation facility used in international air navigation` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(e)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): paragraph 77(e)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(b)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d): paragraph 77(b)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(f)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d): paragraph 77(f)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(d) at or in relation to an airport serving international civil aviation` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(e)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- 77(e) belongs to paragraph (c), not (d)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(a)` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no circumstance of (a) to (d)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(a)` `ccc1 test conspiracy` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): a conspiracy to commit an offence referred to in the subsection, whatever the circumstance
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test paragraph 77(h)` `ccc1 test attempt` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- 77(h) is not referred to in the subsection
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test whole section 77` `ccc1 test attempt` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- only paragraphs 77(a) to (g) are named, so a whole-section reference is not one of them
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test accessory` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): being an accessory after the fact
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2) none of those circumstances` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test counselling` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e): counselling
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test no relation` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relation to the offence
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` FALSE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- committed in Canada: the subsection is about acts outside Canada
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `s 7(2)(a) on an aircraft, while the aircraft is in flight` `ccc1 test section 76` `ccc1 test itself` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person is not present in Canada afterwards: "if the person is, after the commission thereof, present in Canada"

§ `s 7(2.01)  (outside Canada; offence; relation; cultural property; grounds)`
`ccc1 test 322` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 322, ""
`ccc1 test 321` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 321, ""
`ccc1 test 323` MEANS `Provision of the Code` OF 323, ""
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a): a Canadian citizen
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(b) the person is not a citizen of any state and ordinarily resides in Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(c) the person is a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act and is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none of (a) to (c): "is deemed ... if the person"
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 341, "") `ccc1 test conspiracy` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 341, a conspiracy to commit it
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 344, "") `ccc1 test attempt` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 344, an attempt
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 380, "") `ccc1 test accessory` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 380, accessory after the fact
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 430, "") `ccc1 test counselling` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 430, counselling
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 434, "") `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 434, the last section named
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 321` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 321 is not one of the six sections
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 323` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 323 is not one of the six sections
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test no relation` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relation to the offence
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` FALSE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in relation to cultural property as defined in Article 1
#ASSERT `s 7(2.01) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` FALSE `ccc1 test 322` `ccc1 test itself` TRUE (LIST `s 7(2.01)(a) the person is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- committed in Canada

§ `s 7(2.02)  (the Convention)`
#ASSERT `s 7(2.02) the instrument is the Convention` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the Convention done at The Hague on May 14, 1954
#ASSERT `s 7(2.02) the instrument is the Convention` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Convention means ..."
#ASSERT `s 7(2.02) where Article 1 of the Convention is set out` EQUALS "the schedule to the Cultural Property Export and Import Act"   -- the text's own pointer

§ `s 7(2.1)  (outside Canada; the place; offence; relation; grounds)`
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(b) the act or omission is committed against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(d) the act or omission is committed by a person who is not a citizen of any state and who ordinarily resides in Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(e) the act or omission is committed by a person who is, after the commission of the offence, present in Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(f) the act or omission is committed in such a way as to seize, injure or kill, or threaten to injure or kill, a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (f)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(g) the act or omission is committed in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (g)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- none of (a) to (g)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test conspiracy` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a conspiracy to commit an offence against section 78.1
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test no relation` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relation to the offence
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 78, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 78 is not section 78.1
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 78.2, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- nor is section 78.2
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE FALSE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not against or on board a platform or ship beyond the territorial sea
#ASSERT `s 7(2.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` FALSE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- committed in Canada

§ `s 7(2.2)  (outside Canada; the place; offence; relation; the ways of (2.1); the state where the offender is found)`
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(b) the act or omission is committed against or on board a ship registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, pursuant to any Act of Parliament`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) by way of (2.1)(b) and (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(g) the act or omission is committed in an attempt to compel the Government of Canada to do or refrain from doing any act`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(ii) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Protocol for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Fixed Platforms Located on the Continental Shelf, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a fixed platform` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) by way of (2.1)(g) and (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- only paragraph (2.1)(a) holds: "any of paragraphs (2.1)(b) to (g)" is not met
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(a) the act or omission is committed against or on board a fixed platform attached to the continental shelf of Canada`, `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (2.1)(c) is among the ways
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b) a state that is none of those` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) is not met: both paragraphs are required ("and")
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` EMPTY `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) is not met
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE FALSE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the platform is attached to the continental shelf, or the ship navigates beyond the territorial sea: that is (2.1)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 78, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS NOTHING   -- not section 78.1
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test attempt` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an attempt is covered
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test no relation` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relation to the offence
#ASSERT `s 7(2.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` FALSE TRUE `ccc1 test section 78.1` `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.1)(c) the act or omission is committed by a Canadian citizen`) `s 7(2.2)(b)(i) a state, other than the state in which the act or omission was committed, that is a party to the Convention for the Suppression of Unlawful Acts against the Safety of Maritime Navigation, done at Rome on March 10, 1988, in respect of an offence committed against or on board a ship` EQUALS NOTHING   -- committed in Canada

§ `s 7(2.21)  (outside Canada; offence; relation; grounds)`
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.3, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(a) the act or omission is committed on a ship that is registered or licensed, or for which an identification number has been issued, under any Act of Parliament`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 82.3, the first section of the range; ground (a)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.6, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(b)(i) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft that is registered in Canada under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 82.6, the last section of the range; ground (b)(i)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.4, "") `ccc1 test conspiracy` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(b)(ii) the act or omission is committed on an aircraft that is leased without crew and operated by a person who is qualified under regulations made under the Aeronautics Act to be registered as owner of an aircraft in Canada under those regulations`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 82.4, conspiracy; ground (b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.5, "") `ccc1 test accessory` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 82.5, accessory after the fact; ground (c)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.5, "") `ccc1 test counselling` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(d) the person who commits the act or omission is, after the commission of the act or omission, present in Canada`) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- counselling; ground (d)
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.4, "") `ccc1 test attempt` EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no ground: "is deemed ... if"
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.2, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 82.2 is before 82.3
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.7, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 82.7 is after 82.6
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.4, "") `ccc1 test no relation` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no relation
#ASSERT `s 7(2.21) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 82.4, "") `ccc1 test itself` (LIST `s 7(2.21)(c) the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen`) EQUALS NOTHING   -- committed in Canada
